# energyDataCapture
# Local mirror of the container's mounted volume (PLAN.md §5): spool.db,
# tokens/*.json, status.json. Runtime state, never source.
/data/
spool.db
spool.db-wal
spool.db-shm
status.json
# Cached API tokens are secrets (mode 600, volume-only — CLAUDE.md rule 8).
tokens/
# Parquet is warehouse output; it lives in S3, not in git.
*.parquet
# `energycap discover` output, written beside the committed channel_map.json.
# Regenerated on every run and specific to one house's hardware (hub ids, the
# system serial), so it is state, not source. build-dim reads whatever is there.
config/live_channels.json
# The raw-response dump (`energycap discover --dump FILE`, mode 600): complete
# upstream bodies, captured for fixtures. Trim what you need into
# tests/fixtures/ by hand; never commit the dump itself.
discover-raw*.json
# NOTE: .env, .venv/ and __pycache__/ are already ignored above.
# NOTE: uv.lock is deliberately NOT ignored — it must be committed, because the
# Dockerfile builds with `uv sync --frozen` and will fail without it.
